  "name": "Sea State, Surface Weather, Upper-level Winds, Evaporation Power, Air Masses, and Monsoon Weather for Asia",
  "description": "Publication Title: Tropical Climatology and forecasting in the Far East. Includes a summarized narrative of air masses, pressure, surface winds (with reference to the doldrums), upper winds, cloud, precipitation, visibility, temperature, relative humidity, evaporation power, icing, turbulence, sea and swell, and weather of the monsoons. Data are for the Far East. Includes bibliographical references. Available from the NOAA Library System: URL http://www.lib.noaa.gov/.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This publication is in the National Climatic Data Center's Foreign Data Library, and is one of many books, atlases, maps, charts and other printed materials received by the NCDC from many nations over the years.",
